  "extractionNotes": "Self-employed mother on preferential contributions (declared base 1441.80 every month 2026-01..07, below 60% of the forecast wage) with voluntary sickness insurance from 2026-01-01; child born 2026-08-05. She first sent only a Z-3b with the benefit period; ZUS wrote on 2026-08-12 asking for a ZAM within 14 days. The ZAM asks for maternity benefit only until 2026-11-10, i.e. the mother ends maternity leave after the minimum 14 weeks (98 days) and claims no parental leave; she wrote the birth date in the adoption field by mistake. ZUS memo (study date 2026-08-05): no arrears; social and sickness insurance deregistered from 2026-08-05 because of the concurrence with maternity benefit (kept open here, as in the pilots, because the benefit itself causes it); after the benefit, health insurance until 2026-11-10 and pension/accident insurance again from 2026-11-11 (back to business). Benefit screen: 2026-08-05..2026-11-10, 98 days, 100%; handwritten note: maternity benefit granted for that period. The ZUS memo request quoted the end as 2026-11-11. Base not printed (about 1244.13 from 1441.80 less 13.71%). asOf = date of the ZUS letter (the ZAM date is not legible)."
